Subject: [PATCH 6/9] A course has a question bank, and a student sees the
 answer only after submitting

The seven practice tables and seventeen doors: the bank (drafts a teacher
may write for a quick check, approval by whoever manages the course),
sets, assignments (quiet in a lesson, a push at home), attempts with one
open per assignment, answers marked in SQL by the room's own rules ported
line for line (mcq, multi-select with partial credit, numeric with the
half-unit default, short text normalised; worked waits for a person),
the integrity log a student can only append to, the review for a flagged
test, and the two private buckets. Students and families never read the
question table; a question reaches a student through attempt_questions,
which hides the key until the attempt is submitted. A resume carries its
pause, so the clock allows for it while the test is still open.

