+-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+-- A course has a question bank and a student sees the answer only after
+-- submitting (migration 20261013170702; CONTRACTS-stage4.md section B)
+--
+-- The bank is the in-charge's: a teacher cannot put a question in it, a
+-- student never selects it at all (drafts, approved or retired, with an
+-- attempt in hand or not), and a teacher with a lesson on the course this
+-- fortnight reads only the approved rows. The marking is the room's, so the
+-- room's own test file (online-lms/tests/practice-marking.test.ts) is
+-- replayed here against the SQL, case by case. A set is made by whoever
+-- manages the course, or -- a quick check -- by the host of a live lesson,
+-- who may give it only to that lesson's student, quietly; a set to do at
+-- home reaches the push queue once per student. The student it was given
+-- to starts the attempt and nobody else, not a sibling; the key and the
+-- worked solution are null while the attempt is open and shown after
+-- submission unless the set hides them; an answer after the time is up,
+-- and an integrity event after submission, are refused. A parent reads the
+-- attempt row and never the answers or the integrity events; the assigner,
+-- the course and an admin read all three. The two buckets follow the same
+-- lines: a snapshot is written under the student's own prefix and read by
+-- its owner and by whoever may review the attempt; a question's picture is
+-- written by the course and read by the student who has it in front of
+-- them.
+-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+begin;
+set local role postgres;
+select set_config('request.jwt.claim.sub', '', true);
+
